R2-1 collision-invariant check: NN Euclidean KG band, d=3 spatial, m=0.50
samples: 3000 real 2->2 shell points (sampler fraction umklapp = 0.65; sampler, not invariant measure)
(C3) w as charge: max |sum_in w - sum_out w| = 2.22e-15
(C2) tau = sawtooth k_1: max|res| non-umklapp rows = 1.78e-15 ; umklapp rows: |res|/2pi values = [0. 1.]
(C1) local non-umklapp sample (800 rows), tau = k_1: max|res| = 8.88e-16
odd finite-range charges tau = sum_n c_n sin(n.k), |n|_inf <= R, unit slope d tau_1/dk_1(0) = 1:
  R  #basis  min RMS residual (unit slope)   smallest sing. value of A/sqrt(rows)   [local-only sample, unit slope]
  1     13   4.1940e-01                     1.2362e+00                              2.0191e-02
  2     62   9.2944e-02                     9.6322e-01                              1.2638e-03
  3    171   3.1073e-02                     7.3668e-01                              3.9519e-05
Reading: on the full shell (umklapp included) no odd finite-range unit-slope charge is an
invariant and the miss does not go to zero with R; locally (no umklapp) the miss shrinks with R
because sin-polynomials approximate k_1 near 0. The obstruction is periodicity + umklapp
(equivalently analyticity + periodicity), not the specific dispersion.

Normalization matters: unit slope at the single point k=0 admits oscillatory charges
(e.g. sin(N k_1)/N) whose residual falls with R; that is not a momentum. Two physical
normalizations follow.
(N1) Fourier truncations of the lattice momentum (sawtooth k_1), tau_R = sum_{n<=R} 2(-1)^{n+1} sin(n k_1)/n:
   R    RMS res (all rows)   RMS res (non-umklapp rows)   RMS res (umklapp rows)
